            "mimeType": "text/html; charset=UTF-8",
            "text": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\" prefix=\"og: https://ogp.me/ns#\" class=\"sticky-header-html\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n<script type=\"text/javascript\" id=\"Cookiebot\" src=\"https://consent.cookiebot.com/uc.js\" data-cbid=\"ec6463a5-adc8-4770-a33a-2161a238e881\" data-blockingmode=\"auto\" async=\"async\"></script>\n<noscript><style>form.antibot * :not(.antibot-message) { display: none !important; }</style>\n</noscript><meta name=\"description\" content=\"🚩 PEOPLE&#039;S EMERGENCY BRIEFING 🚩 What do the changing climate and decline in nature really mean for everyday life in the UK? This FREE community film screening of the People’s Emergency Briefing includes experts explaining the impact on: Extreme weather Food security Health Cost of living This event is open to everyone, and the film will be followed by a facilitated group discussion, including how to be part of the solutions, collectively and individually.\" />\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://haringey.gov.uk/events/free-film-screening-harringay-peoples-emergency-briefing\" />\n<meta name=\"Generator\" content=\"Drupal 10 (LocalGov Drupal | https://localgovdrupal.org)\" />\n<meta name=\"MobileOptimized\" content=\"width\" />\n<meta name=\"HandheldFriendly\" content=\"true\" />\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n<link rel=\"icon\" href=\"/core/misc/favicon.ico\" type=\"image/vnd.microsoft.icon\" />\n\n    <title>Free film screening in Harringay – People&#039;s Emergency Briefing | Haringey Council</title>\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" media=\"all\" href=\"/sites/default/files/css/css_rqTIsa0z9d6ZoOv0l167vPYS3IiXkJHPYijhnn6Kwjc.css?delta=0&amp;language=en&amp;theme=lgd&amp;include=eJxtkNGWgyAMRH8I5ZM8AUZkDeBJ0G7_frXHbbd2X5jM3DxMoCJtiGERS7-Toc9s8LXOCa62nba0qz21H6tk88T2teirwAZZF-KevujbjLU0ukFrhv0z9ze4w6qZ2PlhBIIjP9s3NziufjYMGhnNRhQI8dOf2o8rs3oBygeK0LYKholK4FSi4RgsNpTWBWrQl9dO2_25ItClFk0bukaOz0UFiZ_OUtUTx7oNjhTWCSh